{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the equation \\(\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} = \\frac{2}{17}\\) for positive integers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), we start by finding a common denominator for the left side of the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a + b}{ab} = \\frac{2}{17}\n\\]\n\nThis implies that:\n\n\\[\n17(a + b) = 2ab\n\\]\n\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n2ab - 17a - 17b = 0\n\\]\n\nTo solve this, we add 289 to both sides to facilitate factoring:\n\n\\[\n2ab - 17a - 17b + 289 = 289\n\\]\n\nThis can be factored as:\n\n\\[\n(2a - 17)(b - \\frac{17}{2}) = \\frac{289}{2}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 to clear the fraction, we get:\n\n\\[\n(2a - 17)(2b - 17) = 289\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find all pairs of factors of 289. Since \\(289 = 17^2\\), the factor pairs of 289 are \\((1, 289)\\), \\((17, 17)\\), and \\((289, 1)\\). We will solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) using each pair.\n\n1. For the pair \\((1, 289)\\):\n\n","prefix_end":823,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,23606,1124,11520,37018,90,16,15170,64,92,488,1124,37018,90,16,15170,65,92,284,1124,37018,90,17,15170,16,22,11035,8,369,6785,25780,17767,64,57758,323,17767,65,59,701,582,1191,553,9271,264,4185,46912,369,279,2115,3108,315,279,23606,1447,59,9640,59,37018,90,64,488,293,15170,370,92,284,1124,37018,90,17,15170,16,22,532,59,2533,1986,23945,429,1447,59,9640,16,22,2877,488,293,8,284,220,17,370,198,59,2533,49,682,81,8595,279,3793,11,582,633,1447,59,9640,17,370,481,220,16,22,64,481,220,16,22,65,284,220,15,198,59,2533,1249,11625,419,11,582,912,220,17,23,24,311,2176,11067,311,27596,2097,5503,1447,59,9640,17,370,481,220,16,22,64,481,220,16,22,65,488,220,17,23,24,284,220,17,23,24,198,59,2533,1986,646,387,2097,3018,438,1447,59,9640,7,17,64,481,220,16,22,2376,65,481,1124,37018,90,16,22,15170,17,5410,284,1124,37018,90,17,23,24,15170,17,532,59,2533,57251,6711,2176,11067,553,220,